{"type":"message","id":"518d48f5","parentId":"4286ee85","timestamp":"2026-05-22T07:23:34.476Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_YWMTA4WeciPjpRd7GxZX3mme","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const fs = require('fs');\n\nfunction parse(file, site) {\n  try {\n    const data = fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\n    const regex = /<item>[\\s\\S]*?<title>(.*?)<\\/title>[\\s\\S]*?<link>(.*?)<\\/link>[\\s\\S]*?<pubDate>(.*?)<\\/pubDate>[\\s\\S]*?<\\/item>/g;\n    let match;\n    let limit = 20;\n    while ((match = regex.exec(data)) && limit > 0) {\n      if (match[3].includes(\"29 Apr 2026\") || match[3].includes(\"28 Apr 2026\")) {\n        console.log(`${site}|${match[1]}|${match[3]}|${match[2]}`);\n      }\n      limit--;\n    }\n  } catch(e) {}\n}\n\nparse('coindesk.xml', 'CoinDesk');\nparse('cointelegraph.xml', 'CoinTelegraph');\nparse('decrypt.xml', 'Decrypt');\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779434614476}}
{"type":"message","id":"f875950e","parentId":"518d48f5","timestamp":"2026-05-22T07:23:34.476Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_B5TrSBQ0UbIaxC94zbHO8uk8","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const fs = require('fs');\n\nfunction parse(file, site) {\n  try {\n    const data = fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\n    const regex = /<item>[\\s\\S]*?<title>(.*?)<\\/title>[\\s\\S]*?<link>(.*?)<\\/link>[\\s\\S]*?<pubDate>(.*?)<\\/pubDate>[\\s\\S]*?<\\/item>/g;\n    let match;\n    let limit = 20;\n    while ((match = regex.exec(data)) && limit > 0) {\n      if (match[3].includes(\"29 Apr 2026\") || match[3].includes(\"28 Apr 2026\")) {\n        console.log(`${site}|${match[1]}|${match[3]}|${match[2]}`);\n      }\n      limit--;\n    }\n  } catch(e) {}\n}\n\nparse('coindesk.xml', 'CoinDesk');\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779434614476}}
{"type":"message","id":"9518ca1c","parentId":"f875950e","timestamp":"2026-05-22T07:23:34.476Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_w2FOtgnORrkzVARKdocE9q6s","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"SBI Holdings' Potential Acquisition of Bitbank\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"SBI Bitbank acquisition\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"SBI to Make Bitbank a Subsidiary in Japan Crypto Consolidation Push\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"CoinTelegraph\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/sbi-seeks-to-make-bitbank-a-subsidiary-in-japan-crypto-consolidation-push\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"Tokyo-based SBI Holdings has opened talks to acquire shares in cryptocurrency exchange Bitbank and make it a consolidated subsidiary.\",\n    \"The move is part of SBI's push to consolidate regulated crypto trading platforms in Japan.\",\n    \"The potential deal would help the group establish an “overwhelming position in the domestic cryptocurrency industry.”\",\n    \"Japan’s Cabinet approved a bill on April 10 to amend the Financial Instruments and Exchange Act and the Payment Services Act, strengthening crypto market fairness, transparency, and investor protection.\",\n    \"Bitbank is one of Japan’s major crypto exchanges, ranking as the leading cryptocurrency exchange by Coingecko’s trust score.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: SBI to Make Bitbank a Subsidiary in Japan Crypto Consolidation Push\\n\\nURL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/sbi-seeks-to-make-bitbank-a-subsidiary-in-japan-crypto-consolidation-push\\n\\nPublished Time: Fri, 01 May 2026 11:17:45 GMT\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\nTokyo-based SBI Holdings has opened talks to acquire shares in cryptocurrency exchange Bitbank and make it a consolidated subsidiary, extending its push to consolidate regulated crypto trading platforms in Japan as the country moves toward securities-style rules for digital assets.\\n\\nThe financial conglomerate [said](https://www.sbigroup.co.jp/news/2026/0501_16298.html) Friday it is considering a share acquisition as part of a potential capital and business alliance with Bitbank. The deal remains subject to due diligence, negotiations and internal approvals, SBI said.\\n\\nThe talks come a month after SBI VC Trade [absorbed](https://www.sbivc.co.jp/newsview/umhk6419ku) Bitpoint Japan on April 1, with SBI VC Trade becoming the surviving company. A Bitbank acquisition would give SBI a larger position in Japan’s crypto exchange market at a time when policymakers are preparing to bring crypto assets under the Financial Instruments and Exchange Act.\\n\\nSBI said the potential deal would help the group establish an “overwhelming position in the domestic cryptocurrency industry,” citing Japan’s planned regulatory shift for crypto assets.\\n\\nJapan’s Cabinet approved a bill on April 10 to [amend the Financial Instruments and Exchange Act](https://cointelegraph.com/news/japan-approves-bill-classify-cryptocurrencies-financial-instruments) and the Payment Services Act, according to the Financial Services Agency. The bill is intended to strengthen market fairness, transparency and investor protection while revising rules for crypto assets.\\n\\nCrypto assets are currently regulated by the FSA under the Payment Services Act as a means of payment. The proposed changes would move crypto closer to Japan’s traditional financial market framework, with stronger disclosure, exchange oversight and rules targeting unfair trading.\\n\\nCointelegraph asked SBI Holdings for comment on the proposed Bitbank acquisition and how Japan’s shifting crypto rules are affecting the group’s exchange strategy, but had not received a response by publication.\\n\\n![Image 1](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=896,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/pasted-image-222.png?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_Bitbank company profile. Source: SBI Group_\\n\\nBitbank is one of Japan’s major crypto exchanges. It [ranks](https://www.coingecko.com/en/exchanges/country/japan) as Japan’s leading cryptocurrency exchange by Coingecko’s trust score, which measures the legitimacy of crypto exchanges based on liquidity, trading activity, cybersecurity and operational scale.\\n\\nIt ranks third among cryptocurrency exchanges by daily trading volume, behind bitFlyer and Coincheck.\\n\\n![Image 2](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=896,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/pasted-image-223.png?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_Top Japanese crypto exchanges by trust score. Source: Coingecko_\\n\\nThe proposed deal would add to SBI’s broader digital asset footprint. SBI made a $50 million investment in Circle's IPO in June 2025. In previous years, SBI also made strategic investments in other crypto-native companies, including BITPoint Japan, Sygnum Bank and crypto exchange TaoTao, which later merged into SBI VC Trade.\\n\\n## Japan brings crypto under TradFi umbrella, targets ETFs by 2028\\n\\nJapan’s regulatory shift comes as institutional interest in digital assets continues to grow and policymakers reassess how crypto should fit within the country’s financial markets.\\n\\nJapanese Finance Minister Satsuki Katayama first [signaled](https://cointelegraph.com/news/japan-crypto-securities-framework-exchange-led-access-2026) the intent to bring crypto under the same umbrella as traditional finance assets in January, to ensure that citizens will “benefit from digital and blockchain-based assets.”\\n\\n_**Related:**_[_**South Korea’s Shinhan Card taps Solana to test real-world stablecoin payments**_](https://cointelegraph.com/news/south-korean-credit-card-giant-partners-with-solana-for-stablecoin-payments-defi-infrastructure)\\n\\nThe country is also planning to legalize the launch of cryptocurrency exchange-traded funds (ETFs) by 2028, [according](https://cointelegraph.com/news/japan-considers-crypto-etfs-2028-nikkei) to a January report. Large financial conglomerates like SBI Holdings and Nomura are among the first companies expected to [develop crypto-linked ETFs](https://cointelegraph.com/news/sbi-plans-bitcoin-xrp-etf-japan).\\n\\n_**Magazine:**_[_**Singapore isn’t a ‘crypto hub’ — it’s something better: StraitsX CEO**_](https://cointelegraph-magazine.com/singapore-crypto-speculation-down-mas-loophole-closure-asia-express/)\\n\\nCointelegraph\"\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779434614476}}
{"type":"message","id":"0424b5e9","parentId":"9518ca1c","timestamp":"2026-05-22T07:23:41.005Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2NxOqE7f3YHbdwg99AeZPO7k","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"set -e\nfile /tmp/researcher-raw.txt 2>/dev/null || true\nprintf '\\n---\\n'\nls -l /tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research 2>/dev/null || true\nprintf '\\n---\\n'\nnode -v\nprintf '\\n---\\n'\nfor u in 'https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/' 'https://cointelegraph.com/rss' 'https://decrypt.co/feed' 'https://www.theblock.co/rss.xml'; do echo \"URL $u\"; curl -L --max-time 20 -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -s \"$u\" | head -n 12; echo; echo '===='; done","yieldMs":4000}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":12531,"output":398,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":12929,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779434614477,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DiEWGDDZS0Fn1ku6c51QcxzQ4gnbA"}}
