uejNIX2k5NEFZeElacXRJYVEzeVZLMFNLSERSZGZqelk4R19YNWtianVybFdHU05mZ2dqUDJyZUF3bzRsWHlrV19vaTBSUVBWRzFkNDUyc3RLUl9zSU5KY1E</guid><pubDate>Fri, 22 May 2026 03:26:25 GMT</pubDate><description>&lt;a href=\"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMidkFVX3lxTE5ZaFg3bGN4ZEFwaEVCZzVMOVFEVVJuejNIX2k5NEFZeElacXRJYVEzeVZLMFNLSERSZGZqelk4R19YNWtianVybFdHU05mZ2dqUDJyZUF3bzRsWHlrV19vaTBSUVBWRzFkNDUyc3RLUl9zSU5KY1E?oc=5\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;ETH/USDT&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;font color=\"#6f6f6f\"&gt;Binance&lt;/font&gt;</description><source url=\"https://www.binance.com\">Binance</source></item><item><title>ETH/USDT - Binance</title><link>https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMidkFVX3lxTE85X2YtUTNfUmpMUExVVXUzWDZkMVprY0JKb1J0Sm16NVNnMTJFYlVlZ1Z0TVB1Rjh6X1lvQkRyLW53eTdwZndhUzRpMzEzV182bUo0bmpSWm14Z2NfNWFHLVk0MDJXT0V1OG85bGFMQnhBV0NyRFE?oc=5</link><guid isPermaLink=\"false\">CBMidkFVX3lxTE85X2YtUTNfUmpMUExVVXUzWDZkMVprY0JKb1J0Sm16NVNnMTJFYlVlZ1Z0TVB1Rjh6X1lvQkRyLW53eTdwZndhUzRpMzEzV182bUo0bmpSWm14Z2NfNWFHLVk0MDJXT0V1OG85bGFMQnhBV0NyRFE</guid><pubDate>Fri, 22 May 2026 04:28:20 GMT</pubDate><description>&lt;a href=\"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMidkFVX3lxTE85X2YtUTNfUmpMUExVVXUzWDZkMVprY0JKb1J0Sm16NVNnMTJFYlVlZ1Z0TVB1Rjh6X1lvQkRyLW53eTdwZndhUzRpMzEzV182bUo0bmpSWm14Z2NfNWFHLVk0MDJXT0V1OG85bGFMQnhBV0NyRFE?oc=5\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;ETH/USDT&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;font color=\"#6f6f6f\"&gt;Binance&lt;/font&gt;</description><source url=\"https://www.binance.com\">Binance</source></item></channel></rss>\n\n===== ARMA =====\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml:81:      <title>US lawmakers renew strategic Bitcoin reserve push with ARMA bill</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml:86:      <description><![CDATA[<p style=\"float:right; margin:0 0 10px 15px; width:240px;\"><img src=\"https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy1pbWFnZXMuY3RtZWRpYS5pby9tZWRpYS9hcnRpY2xlLWNvdmVycy9oaS1uZXctdXMtY2hpZWYtb2Ytc3RhZmYtc3VwcG9ydHMtYml0Y29pbjEuanBn.jpg\" alt=\"US lawmakers renew strategic Bitcoin reserve push with ARMA bill\" class=\"type:primaryImage\"></p><p>Under the American Reserve Modernization Act of 2026, Bitcoin must be held for a minimum of 20 years unless used to slash national debt.</p>]]></description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml:178:<p>The Treasury’s investigation revealed a sophisticated structure designed to move large sums of capital across borders while attempting to evade traditional banking oversight. The sanctioned individuals, led by <strong>Armando de Jesus Ojeda Aviles</strong>, orchestrated a system that integrated physical cash collection with digital transfers. <em>The process typically involved \"smurfing\" or the use of couriers to gather bulk currency before converting it into crypto assets for international transmission.</em></p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:174:\t\t\t\t\t<description><![CDATA[<p>A renewed push to solidify the United States’ foothold in the digital asset market emerged Thursday as lawmakers unveiled legislation to establish a formal strategic Bitcoin reserve and consolidate the federal government's multibillion-dollar cryptocurrency stockpile. Spearheaded by Representative Nick Begich, the American Reserve Modernization Act (ARMA) of 2026 mandates the creation of a secure Bitcoin [&#8230;]</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:178:<p>Spearheaded by Representative Nick Begich, the American Reserve Modernization Act (ARMA) of 2026 mandates the creation of a secure <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/is-the-eu-bitcoin-race-starting-france-targets-420k-btc-as-germany-weighs-reserves/\">Bitcoin reserve</a> within the US Department of the Treasury, alongside a separate “Digital Asset Stockpile” for federally held, non-Bitcoin cryptocurrencies.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:186:<h2>ARMA establishes a 20-year Bitcoin bet</h2>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml:350:  <title>Proposed ARMA Bill Aims to Enshrine Strategic Bitcoin Reserve Into Law</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml:351:  <link>https://decrypt.co/368662/proposed-arma-bill-aims-enshrine-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-law</link>\n\n===== Strategic Bitcoin Reserve =====\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml:81:      <title>US lawmakers renew strategic Bitcoin reserve push with ARMA bill</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml:86:      <description><![CDATA[<p style=\"float:right; margin:0 0 10px 15px; width:240px;\"><img src=\"https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy1pbWFnZXMuY3RtZWRpYS5pby9tZWRpYS9hcnRpY2xlLWNvdmVycy9oaS1uZXctdXMtY2hpZWYtb2Ytc3RhZmYtc3VwcG9ydHMtYml0Y29pbjEuanBn.jpg\" alt=\"US lawmakers renew strategic Bitcoin reserve push with ARMA bill\" class=\"type:primaryImage\"></p><p>Under the American Reserve Modernization Act of 2026, Bitcoin must be held for a minimum of 20 years unless used to slash national debt.</p>]]></description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml:61:    <title>US Lawmakers Introduce Bill to Establish Strategic Bitcoin Reserve</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml:65:    <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>US Representative <strong>Nick Begich</strong> has introduced the <strong>Reserve Modernization Act</strong>, a legislative proposal designed to formalize the role of digital assets within the national treasury. Supported by <strong>16 original co-sponsors</strong>, the bill seeks to establish a permanent <strong>strategic Bitcoin reserve</strong>, integrating federally held digital assets into a long-term storage framework. This initiative marks a significant shift in federal fiscal policy, aiming to treat <strong>BTC</strong> as a cornerstone of the nation's financial security for the coming decades.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml:101:    <title>US Lawmakers Introduce Bill to Establish Strategic Bitcoin Reserve</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml:105:    <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>US Representative <strong>Nick Begich</strong> has introduced the <strong>Reserve Modernization Act</strong>, a legislative proposal designed to formalize the role of digital assets within the national treasury. Supported by <strong>16 original co-sponsors</strong>, the bill seeks to establish a permanent <strong>strategic Bitcoin reserve</strong>, integrating federally held digital assets into a long-term storage framework. This initiative marks a significant shift in federal fiscal policy, aiming to treat <strong>BTC</strong> as a cornerstone of the nation's financial security for the coming decades.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:157:\t\t<title>US lawmakers push new Strategic Bitcoin Reserve act to secure $25 billion federal stash</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:174:\t\t\t\t\t<description><![CDATA[<p>A renewed push to solidify the United States’ foothold in the digital asset market emerged Thursday as lawmakers unveiled legislation to establish a formal strategic Bitcoin reserve and consolidate the federal government's multibillion-dollar cryptocurrency stockpile. Spearheaded by Representative Nick Begich, the American Reserve Modernization Act (ARMA) of 2026 mandates the creation of a secure Bitcoin [&#8230;]</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:175:<p>The post <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/us-lawmakers-push-new-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-act-to-secure-25-billion-federal-stash/\">US lawmakers push new Strategic Bitcoin Reserve act to secure $25 billion federal stash</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com\">CryptoSlate</a>.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:192:<p><a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/bitocin-20yr-hold-comic.jpg\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-537707 size-full\" src=\"https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/bitocin-20yr-hold-comic.jpg\" alt=\"Uncle Sam placing a Bitcoin coin into a 20-year hold vault for a Strategic Bitcoin Reserve.\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" srcset=\"https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/bitocin-20yr-hold-comic.jpg 1280w, https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/bitocin-20yr-hold-comic-300x169.jpg 300w, https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/bitocin-20yr-hold-comic-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/bitocin-20yr-hold-comic-768x432.jpg 768w, https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/bitocin-20yr-hold-comic-480x270.jpg 480w, https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/bitocin-20yr-hold-comic-1200x675.jpg 1200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\" /></a></p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:197:<p>Lummis legislation followed President <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/people/donald-trump/\">Donald Trump's</a> executive <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/trumps-signs-bitcoin-reserve-order-but-wont-buy-more-for-now/\">order to establish a strategic Bitcoin reserve. </a></p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:200:<p>The post <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/us-lawmakers-push-new-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-act-to-secure-25-billion-federal-stash/\">US lawmakers push new Strategic Bitcoin Reserve act to secure $25 billion federal stash</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com\">CryptoSlate</a>.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml:350:  <title>Proposed ARMA Bill Aims to Enshrine Strategic Bitcoin Reserve Into Law</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml:1616:    <description>Crypto majors are red while Gold nears $5,000 and Silver closes in on $100; BTC -1% at $89,100; ETH -2% at $2,925, SOL -2% at $127; XRP -2% to $1.90. ZRO (+15%), AXS (+10%) and DASH (+8%) led top movers. Ledger is preparing for a $4B IPO, enlisting Goldman Sachs, Jefferies and Barclays for support. Ripple CEO Brad Garlinghouse predicted crypto could hit new highs in 2026, pointing to regulatory momentum and institutional participation as key drivers. President Trump sued JPMorgan for $5 billion, alleging politically motivated “debanking”. BitGo briefly surged in its stock market debut before finishing its first day of trading just over its $18 IPO price. BlackRock CEO Larry Fink pushed the idea of a single blockchain for tokenization to avoid corruption and aid in scaling. Kansas introduced its own Bitcoin Strategic Reserve bill. PwC said institutional crypto adoption has crossed a point of no return, as regulatory frameworks move from draft rules toward active supervision. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent reaffirmed the Trump administration’s push for U.S. crypto leadership and support for a strategic Bitcoin reserve.</description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml:2074:  <title>ZEC Rebounds 11%! Trump says he won’t pardon Sam Bankman-Fried! Florida revisits it’s Strategic Bitcoin Reserve!</title>\n\n===== quantum =====\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/beincrypto.xml:493:<li><a href=\"https://x.com/WuBlockchain/status/2057638414187680194\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Glassnode estimates </a>6.04 million BTC, worth nearly $500 billion, sit exposed to future quantum computing attack risks.</li>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/beincrypto.xml:931:<p>The appeal is addressed to the Japanese delegates (dReps) who voted against the proposal. The plan would fund post-quantum cryptography, zero-knowledge proofs, and scalability work at Input Output Global (IOG) and partner universities.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/beincrypto.xml:965:<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://assets.beincrypto.com/img/4qdN6padY0F1PPtl6sVBQgKpevw=/smart/945e83160d564d79a675c3e4ac0d0247\" alt=\"Cardano Vision 2026: Human Centred, Scalable, Post Quantum Secure - IO Research o\" class=\"wp-image-831836\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Cardano Vision 2026: Human Centred, Scalable, Post Quantum Secure &ndash; IO Research</figcaption></figure>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/beincrypto.xml:973:<p>It funds work on Ouroboros Leios, <a href=\"https://beincrypto.com/cardano-hoskinson-crypto-quantum-threat-2033/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">post-quantum cryptography</a>, and zero-knowledge proofs. Aggelos Kiayias, IOG&rsquo;s chief scientist, leads the program, with researchers at Edinburgh, Tokyo, Oxford, and Buenos Aires.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/coindesk.xml:67:      <title><![CDATA[Satoshi’s 1.1 million bitcoin and millions more can be saved from quantum attack, says expert]]></title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/coindesk.xml:68:      <link>https://www.coindesk.com/tech/2026/05/21/satoshi-s-1-1m-bitcoin-stash-can-be-saved-from-quantum-attack-says-americanfortress</link>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/coindesk.xml:72:      <description><![CDATA[Researchers at the privacy-centric blockchain startup say their multi-layer quantum defense will feature a soft fork to freeze and protect dormant BTC.]]></description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/coindesk.xml:78:      <category domain=\"tag\"><![CDATA[quantum computing]]></category>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/coindesk.xml:272:      <title><![CDATA[It's not all HYPE: Privacy and quantum-resistant coins advance as bitcoin coasts]]></title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/coindesk.xml:273:      <link>https://www.coindesk.com/daybook-us/2026/05/21/it-s-not-all-hype-privacy-and-quantum-resistant-coins-surge-as-bitcoin-marks-time</link>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:498:\t\t<title>Bitcoin quantum computing risk centers on major exchange wallets, Glassnode data shows</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:499:\t\t<link>https://cryptoslate.com/bitcoin-quantum-computing-risk-exchange-wallets/</link>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:507:\t\t<category><![CDATA[Quantum]]></category>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:512:\t\t<category><![CDATA[quantum computing]]></category>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:515:\t\t\t\t\t<description><![CDATA[<p>Cryptocurrency exchanges are emerging as the clearest pressure point in Bitcoin’s long-running debate over quantum computing risk, sitting on millions of coins with publicly visible cryptographic keys. Bitcoin quantum risk begins with a fundamental feature of its transaction verification: public keys are hidden until funds are spent. Once a wallet signs a transaction, the public [&#8230;]</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:516:<p>The post <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/bitcoin-quantum-computing-risk-exchange-wallets/\">Bitcoin quantum computing risk centers on major exchange wallets, Glassnode data shows</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com\">CryptoSlate</a>.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:518:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Cryptocurrency exchanges are emerging as the clearest pressure point in <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/coins/bitcoin/\">Bitcoin’s</a> long-running debate over quantum computing risk, sitting on millions of coins with publicly visible cryptographic keys.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:519:<p><a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/bitcoin-encryption-isnt-at-risk-from-quantum-computers-for-one-simple-reason-it-doesnt-actually-exist/\">Bitcoin quantum risk</a> begins with a fundamental feature of its transaction verification: public keys are hidden until funds are spent.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:522:<figure id=\"attachment_537395\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-537395\" style=\"width: 1000px\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-537395\" src=\"https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/HIwTSVzXoAAuehh.jpg\" alt=\"Bitcoin SUpply by quantum Safety\" width=\"1000\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/HIwTSVzXoAAuehh.jpg 1000w, https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/HIwTSVzXoAAuehh-300x150.jpg 300w, https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/HIwTSVzXoAAuehh-768x384.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px\" /><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-537395\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Bitcoin Supply by Quantum Safety (Source: Glassnode)</figcaption></figure>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:523:<p>In Glassnode’s framework, public key exposure becomes the core metric for identifying wallets that would matter most in a future quantum-attack scenario.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:524:<p>The data does not imply an immediate threat because quantum computers remain years away from the scale required to break Bitcoin’s encryption.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:525:<p>However, the metric reveals exactly where the network’s vulnerabilities are concentrated if advances in quantum hardware eventually make public-key exposure a practical security concern.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:531:<figure id=\"attachment_537420\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-537420\" style=\"width: 1000px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-537420\" src=\"https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/HIwVBysXQAAM-L3.jpg\" alt=\"Quantum Computing operationally Safe Bitcoin Wallets\" width=\"1000\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/HIwVBysXQAAM-L3.jpg 1000w, https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/HIwVBysXQAAM-L3-300x150.jpg 300w, https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/HIwVBysXQAAM-L3-768x384.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px\" /><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-537420\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Quantum Computing operationally Safe Bitcoin Wallets (Source: Glassnode)</figcaption></figure>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:539:<figure id=\"attachment_537422\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-537422\" style=\"width: 1000px\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-537422\" src=\"https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/HIwUdaKWkAA417o.jpg\" alt=\"Crypto Exchanges Quantum Computing Exposure\" width=\"1000\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/HIwUdaKWkAA417o.jpg 1000w, https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/HIwUdaKWkAA417o-300x150.jpg 300w, https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/HIwUdaKWkAA417o-768x384.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px\" /><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-537422\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Crypto Exchanges Quantum Computing Exposure (Source: Glassnode)</figcaption></figure>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:544:<figure id=\"attachment_537421\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-537421\" style=\"width: 1000px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-537421\" src=\"https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/HIwU2MsWAAIu-9s.jpg\" alt=\"Bitcoin Supply QUantum Exposure by ENtity\" width=\"1000\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/HIwU2MsWAAIu-9s.jpg 1000w, https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/HIwU2MsWAAIu-9s-300x150.jpg 300w, https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/HIwU2MsWAAIu-9s-768x384.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px\" /><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-537421\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Bitcoin Supply Quantum Exposure by Entity (Source: Glassnode)</figcaption></figure>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:545:<p>Government actors, meanwhile, display the strictest cryptographic hygiene of all. Wallets tied to the United States, the United Kingdom, and <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/el-salvador-buys-the-dip-defying-imf-demands-over-100m-in-btc-added-as-price-wobbles/\">El Salvador</a> have maintained zero quantum exposure, boasting safety rates above 99% for several years.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:548:<p>While the timeline for a <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/google-slashes-quantum-cracking-estimates-by-20x-creating-600-billion-quantum-countdown-for-bitcoin-and-ethereum/\">quantum-capable attack</a> remains fiercely debated, Glassnode’s data makes one thing clear: the crypto industry’s most immediate defense lies in basic operational hygiene, not protocol-level overhauls.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:552:<p>Notably, Bitcoin itself cannot be refitted overnight. So any <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/bitcoins-quantum-migration-plan-forces-the-community-to-choose-between-frozen-and-stolen-coins/\">systemic migration to post-quantum signatures</a> would require massive coordination across developers, miners, node operators, wallet providers, and custodians.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:555:<p>As Bitcoin becomes increasingly embedded in spot ETFs, traditional brokerage accounts, and institutional custody products, the first line of defense against future quantum threats will not come from code upgrades, but from the entities holding the largest pools of customer coins.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:557:<p>Bitcoin quantum computing risk is therefore becoming a test of custody before it becomes a protocol-level emergency.</p>\n\n===== prediction markets =====\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/beincrypto.xml:807:\t\t<title>US Regulators Move on Prediction Markets With ETF Pause and NHL Pact</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/beincrypto.xml:820:<p>The post <a href=\"https://beincrypto.com/sec-cftc-prediction-markets-etfs-nhl/\">US Regulators Move on Prediction Markets With ETF Pause and NHL Pact</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://beincrypto.com\">BeInCrypto</a>.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/beincrypto.xml:822:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>Securities and Exchange Commission Chair Paul Atkins said fund sponsors agreed to delay several event contract ETFs tied to prediction markets while the agency seeks public input.</strong></p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/beincrypto.xml:830:<h2 class=\"bic-gutenberg-heading wp-heading wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-parallel-oversight-of-prediction-markets\">Parallel Oversight of Prediction Markets</h2>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/beincrypto.xml:905:<p>The post <a href=\"https://beincrypto.com/sec-cftc-prediction-markets-etfs-nhl/\">US Regulators Move on Prediction Markets With ETF Pause and NHL Pact</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://beincrypto.com\">BeInCrypto</a>.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/coindesk.xml:50:      <title><![CDATA[India cracks down on prediction markets: Polymarket goes dark, Kalshi could be next]]></title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/coindesk.xml:60:      <category domain=\"tag\"><![CDATA[Prediction Markets]]></category>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/coindesk.xml:111:      <title><![CDATA[Crypto prediction markets are turning into dangerous national security risks, and Congress wants to ban them]]></title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/coindesk.xml:121:      <category domain=\"tag\"><![CDATA[Prediction Markets]]></category>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/coindesk.xml:136:      <category domain=\"tag\"><![CDATA[Prediction Markets]]></category>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml:190:      <title>CFTC signs MOU with National Hockey League over prediction markets</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml:195:      <description><![CDATA[<p style=\"float:right; margin:0 0 10px 15px; width:240px;\"><img src=\"https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy1pbWFnZXMuY3RtZWRpYS5pby9tZWRpYS9hcnRpY2xlLWNvdmVycy9oaS1qYXBhbi13aGF0LWlzLWFuLWludmVzdG1lbnQtdHJ1c3QtMi5qcGc=.jpg\" alt=\"CFTC signs MOU with National Hockey League over prediction markets\" class=\"type:primaryImage\"></p><p>The financial regulator signed a similar agreement with Major League Baseball in March and continues to file lawsuits against state-level authorities going after prediction market platforms over sports betting.</p>]]></description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml:50:<ul><li><strong>Projected Timeline:</strong> Full operational status targeted for the year 2030.</li><li><strong>Regulatory Barrier:</strong> Strict anti-gambling laws under the Japanese Penal Code.</li><li><strong>Lobbying Focus:</strong> Reclassifying prediction markets as financial products rather than prohibited gambling.</li></ul>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml:53:<p><em>This regulatory shift could provide a legal pathway for prediction markets if they can be structured as derivatives or regulated financial instruments.</em></p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml:58:<p>In conclusion, Polymarket's long-term commitment to the Japanese market reflects the growing importance of the Asia-Pacific region in the decentralized finance (<strong>DeFi</strong>) sector. While the 2030 goal remains ambitious given Japan's historical stance on digital gambling, the upcoming 2026 financial reforms may offer the necessary clarity for prediction markets to integrate into the country's regulated economy.</p>]]></content:encoded>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml:77:<p>The potential postponement of the vote could prolong the period of <strong>regulatory uncertainty</strong> for issuers of digital assets and blockchain service providers. While prediction markets such as those on Gemini still show high confidence in the bill becoming law by the end of 2026, the immediate focus remains on whether Senate leadership can successfully navigate the crowded June and July schedules to bring the matter to a floor vote.</p>]]></content:encoded>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml:125:<p>The KCSC is currently evaluating the platform's service structure to determine if it breaches the country's strict gambling laws. A primary concern for regulators is that Polymarket offers <strong>Korean language services</strong> and remains accessible within the country without technical barriers such as IP blocking. The commission is reportedly referencing <strong>overseas regulatory cases</strong> to establish a precedent for how decentralized prediction markets should be treated under the law.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml:128:<p>Under South Korean law, unauthorized gambling operations are subject to severe penalties, and the use of <strong>cryptocurrencies</strong> to bypass traditional financial monitoring is an area of increasing scrutiny. <em>Prediction markets differ from traditional betting as they claim to provide \"information aggregation\", yet regulators often view the wagering of assets on uncertain outcomes as a gambling activity.</em> Commission officials have stated that the review process will focus on the nature of the \"bets\" placed and the platform's active efforts to court the local demographic.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml:130:<p>The outcome of this investigation could have significant ramifications for the <strong>Web3 ecosystem</strong> in South Korea. If Polymarket is officially classified as an illegal gambling site, the KCSC may issue orders to <strong>block access</strong> to the domain or demand that the platform implement stricter geo-fencing protocols. As the global regulatory landscape for <strong>DeFi</strong> and prediction markets continues to evolve, this case serves as a critical indicator of how major Asian economies will balance technological innovation with consumer protection laws.</p>]]></content:encoded>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:594:<p>The platform began as a crypto perpetual futures exchange, but has expanded into non-crypto markets, including commodities, equity-linked products, S&P 500 futures, pre-IPO contracts, and prediction markets.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:624:<p>He has pointed to its exposure across crypto, equities, commodities, foreign exchange, prediction markets, and structured products as evidence of a broader market design.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml:268:    <description>The agreement ensures the regulator and the NHL communicate and share data to protect the integrity of hockey-related prediction markets.</description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml:1742:    <description>Crypto majors are very red following a red Tuesday across markets; BTC -3% at $88,200; ETH -6% at $2,905, SOL -2% at $127; XRP -2% to $1.88. MYX (+11%) and ZRO (+10%) led top movers. Bitcoin and Solana both fell below key technical support levels as selling pressure accelerated. Over $1B in longs were liquidated during Bitcoin’s slide below $88k. Delaware Life added Bitcoin exposure to a fixed indexed annuity by linking performance to BlackRock’s spot BTC ETF, one of the first big moves to expand crypto access inside traditional insurance products. Trump Media announced plans to airdrop crypto tokens to shareholders in February, marking its first onchain incentive tied directly to equity ownership. Coinbase CEO Brian Armstrong traveled to Davos to push for a “win-win” U.S. crypto market structure bill amid renewed regulatory momentum. Portugal’s gambling regulator blocked access to Polymarket, citing unlicensed gambling concerns as prediction markets face mounting global scrutiny. The CFTC warned it is underprepared to take on a broader crypto oversight role, as the agency faces staffing shortages after a roughly 21.5% workforce reduction. Galaxy Digital announced plans for a $100M hedge fund targeting crypto and fintech. World Liberty Fi announced its first annual form at Mar-A-Lago on Feb 18.</description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml:1952:    <description>Crypto majors are green; BTC +1.5% at $92,000; ETH +1% at $3,130, SOL +2% at $142; XRP +1% to $2.06. DASH (+60%), IP (+30%) and XMR (+13%) led top movers; XMR hit another new ATH at $680 (now $640). Gold and Silver hit new ATHs again in the wake of the Powell investigation. The US Senate released the draft Crypto Market Clarity Act, including limits on stablecoin rewards. Senator Warren pressed the SEC over inclusion of crypto in 401ks arguing they expose retirees to too much risk. Vitalik Buterin warned crypto needs better decentralized stablecoins, citing governance capture and inflation risks. World Liberty Financial launched a crypto lending platform built around its USD1 stablecoin, attracting ~$20M. BitGo filed for a U.S. IPO targeting a ~$2B valuation as custody assets surpassed $100B. Tennessee regulators ordered Polymarket, Kalshi, and Crypto.com to halt sports prediction markets and refund users, escalating a multi-state legal fight.</description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml:1994:    <description>Crypto majors are green; BTC +1.5% at $92,000; ETH +1% at $3,130, SOL +2% at $142; XRP +1% to $2.06. DASH (+60%), IP (+30%) and XMR (+13%) led top movers; XMR hit another new ATH at $680 (now $640). Gold and Silver hit new ATHs again in the wake of the Powell investigation. The US Senate released the draft Crypto Market Clarity Act, including limits on stablecoin rewards. Senator Warren pressed the SEC over inclusion of crypto in 401ks arguing they expose retirees to too much risk. Vitalik Buterin warned crypto needs better decentralized stablecoins, citing governance capture and inflation risks. World Liberty Financial launched a crypto lending platform built around its USD1 stablecoin, attracting ~$20M. BitGo filed for a U.S. IPO targeting a ~$2B valuation as custody assets surpassed $100B. Tennessee regulators ordered Polymarket, Kalshi, and Crypto.com to halt sports prediction markets and refund users, escalating a multi-state legal fight.</description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml:2036:    <description>Crypto majors are mostly flat headed into Monday open; btc even at $90,600; eth +1% at $3,110, sol +2% at $140; xrp -2% to $2.04. Ip (+20%) and xmr (+15%) led top movers; xmr hit a new ath at $590. Fed chair Jerome Powell released a video message claiming that the criminal charges he faces are due to his not cutting interest rates in line with Trump’s wishes. X (twitter) announced plans for “smart cashtags” to show crypto and stock prices live next to tickers. Vaneck projected bitcoin could reach $53m by 2050, outlining long-term adoption, trade settlement and store-of-value assumptions driving 29% annual growth. Andreessen Horowitz (a16z) raised $15b to fund American Dynanism, with ai and crypto at the forefront. Ripple received FCA approval to scale crypto payments in the uk. Bny mellon debuted tokenized deposits for institutional and digital-native clients. A new house bill would bar lawmakers and federal officials from using prediction markets. Tether froze $182m in usdt linked to Venezuela oil trades.</description>\n\n===== tokenized stocks =====\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml:20:      <title>Tokenized stocks risk liquidity and revenue fragmentation: Research</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml:25:      <description><![CDATA[<p style=\"float:right; margin:0 0 10px 15px; width:240px;\"><img src=\"https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy1pbWFnZXMuY3RtZWRpYS5pby9tZWRpYS9hcnRpY2xlLWNvdmVycy9kaWdpdGFsLWJvbmRzLW9uLWJsb2NrY2hhaW4tMi5qcGc=.jpg\" alt=\"Tokenized stocks risk liquidity and revenue fragmentation: Research\" class=\"type:primaryImage\"></p><p>TradFi views the breakup of its previously consolidated, centralized liquidity as a “serious structural threat,” said Tiger Research director Ryan Yoon.\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml:45:      <title>SEC's Peirce tempers expectations over tokenized stocks exemption</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml:50:      <description><![CDATA[<p style=\"float:right; margin:0 0 10px 15px; width:240px;\"><img src=\"https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy1pbWFnZXMuY3RtZWRpYS5pby9tZWRpYS9hcnRpY2xlLWNvdmVycy9oZXN0ZXItcGVpcmNlLXNlYy5qcGc=.jpg\" alt=\"SEC's Peirce tempers expectations over tokenized stocks exemption\" class=\"type:primaryImage\"></p><p>An executive at tokenization platforms Superstate said the stricter approach suggested by Hester Peirce would enable DeFi to expand without compromising rules in traditional capital markets.</p>]]></description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml:43:    <title>SEC Commissioner Hester Peirce Clarifies Limits on Tokenized Stocks</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml:45:    <description>U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) Commissioner Hester Peirce recently clarified the regulatory boundaries regarding the proposed \"innovation exemption\" for the on-chain trading of tokenized stocks. In a statement released on the social platform X on May 21, 2026, P…</description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml:47:    <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) Commissioner <strong>Hester Peirce</strong> recently clarified the regulatory boundaries regarding the proposed <strong>\"innovation exemption\"</strong> for the on-chain trading of tokenized stocks. In a statement released on the social platform X on May 21, 2026, Peirce addressed what she described as an overinterpretation of the proposal, emphasizing that the exemption is intended to facilitate the digital representation of <strong>existing equity securities</strong> rather than the creation of entirely new financial instruments. This clarification aims to set realistic expectations for the integration of traditional finance and blockchain technology.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml:83:    <title>SEC Commissioner Hester Peirce Clarifies Limits on Tokenized Stocks</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml:85:    <description>U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) Commissioner Hester Peirce recently clarified the regulatory boundaries regarding the proposed \"innovation exemption\" for the on-chain trading of tokenized stocks. In a statement released on the social platform X on May 21, 2026, P…</description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml:87:    <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) Commissioner <strong>Hester Peirce</strong> recently clarified the regulatory boundaries regarding the proposed <strong>\"innovation exemption\"</strong> for the on-chain trading of tokenized stocks. In a statement released on the social platform X on May 21, 2026, Peirce addressed what she described as an overinterpretation of the proposal, emphasizing that the exemption is intended to facilitate the digital representation of <strong>existing equity securities</strong> rather than the creation of entirely new financial instruments. This clarification aims to set realistic expectations for the integration of traditional finance and blockchain technology.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml:339:    <title>SEC to Unveil Innovation Exemption for Tokenized Stocks This Week</title>\n\n===== Mark Cuban =====\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/coindesk.xml:82:      <title><![CDATA[Mark Cuban says he sold most of his Bitcoin after failed hedge narrative 'disappointed' the billionaire]]></title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/coindesk.xml:190:      <title><![CDATA[Live markets: Yet another Iran peace deal and Mark Cuban sells his bitcoin]]></title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml:306:  <title>Mark Cuban Says He Sold Most of His Bitcoin</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml:310:    <description>Outspoken billionaire Mark Cuban is disappointed with Bitcoin&#39;s performance, and said he&#39;s parted ways with most of the BTC in his portfolio.</description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/google.xml:1:<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\" standalone=\"yes\"?><rss version=\"2.0\" xmlns:media=\"http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/\"><channel><generator>NFE/5.0</generator><title>\"cryptocurrency OR blockchain OR eth