{"type":"message","id":"3738cf20","parentId":"fd0a351b","timestamp":"2026-05-22T07:26:16.697Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Jm5408NgHSEC0xrv5XD2W0Fq","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-79-    </item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-80-    <item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml:81:      <title>US lawmakers renew strategic Bitcoin reserve push with ARMA bill</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-82-      <pubDate>Fri, 22 May 2026 04:02:37 +0000</pubDate>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-83-      <atom:updated>Fri, 22 May 2026 04:02:37 +0000</atom:updated>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-84-      <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-senators-unveil-new-bitcoin-bill-renewing-strategic-reserve-plans</guid>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-85-      <link><![CDATA[https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-senators-unveil-new-bitcoin-bill-renewing-strategic-reserve-plans?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound]]></link>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml:86:      <description><![CDATA[<p style=\"float:right; margin:0 0 10px 15px; width:240px;\"><img src=\"https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy1pbWFnZXMuY3RtZWRpYS5pby9tZWRpYS9hcnRpY2xlLWNvdmVycy9oaS1uZXctdXMtY2hpZWYtb2Ytc3RhZmYtc3VwcG9ydHMtYml0Y29pbjEuanBn.jpg\" alt=\"US lawmakers renew strategic Bitcoin reserve push with ARMA bill\" class=\"type:primaryImage\"></p><p>Under the American Reserve Modernization Act of 2026, Bitcoin must be held for a minimum of 20 years unless used to slash national debt.</p>]]></description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-87-      <dc:creator>Cointelegraph by Brayden Lindrea</dc:creator>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-88-      <media:content url=\"https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy1pbWFnZXMuY3RtZWRpYS5pby9tZWRpYS9hcnRpY2xlLWNvdmVycy9oaS1uZXctdXMtY2hpZWYtb2Ytc3RhZmYtc3VwcG9ydHMtYml0Y29pbjEuanBn.jpg\" width=\"528\" medium=\"image\"/>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-89-      <enclosure url=\"https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy1pbWFnZXMuY3RtZWRpYS5pby9tZWRpYS9hcnRpY2xlLWNvdmVycy9oaS1uZXctdXMtY2hpZWYtb2Ytc3RhZmYtc3VwcG9ydHMtYml0Y29pbjEuanBn.jpg\" length=\"528\" type=\"image/jpg\"/>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-90-      <category>Latest News</category>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-91-    </item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-92-    <item>\n--\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml-348-    \n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml-349-      <item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml:350:  <title>Proposed ARMA Bill Aims to Enshrine Strategic Bitcoin Reserve Into Law</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml-351-  <link>https://decrypt.co/368662/proposed-arma-bill-aims-enshrine-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-law</link>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml-352-  <pubDate>Thu, 21 May 2026 18:08:49 +0000</pubDate>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml-353-  \n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml-354-    <description>The American Reserve Modernization Act would direct the Treasury to create and maintain a Bitcoin reserve for a minimum of 20 years.</description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml-355-  \n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml-356-  <dc:creator>André Beganski</dc:creator>\n--\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-155-\t</item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-156-\t\t<item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:157:\t\t<title>US lawmakers push new Strategic Bitcoin Reserve act to secure $25 billion federal stash</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-158-\t\t<link>https://cryptoslate.com/us-lawmakers-push-new-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-act-to-secure-25-billion-federal-stash/</link>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-159-\t\t\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-160-\t\t<dc:creator><![CDATA[Oluwapelumi Adejumo]]></dc:creator>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-161-\t\t<pubDate>Thu, 21 May 2026 19:05:23 +0000</pubDate>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-162-\t\t\t\t<category><![CDATA[Featured]]></category>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-163-\t\t<category><![CDATA[Legislation]]></category>\n--\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-173-\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-174-\t\t\t\t\t<description><![CDATA[<p>A renewed push to solidify the United States’ foothold in the digital asset market emerged Thursday as lawmakers unveiled legislation to establish a formal strategic Bitcoin reserve and consolidate the federal government's multibillion-dollar cryptocurrency stockpile. Spearheaded by Representative Nick Begich, the American Reserve Modernization Act (ARMA) of 2026 mandates the creation of a secure Bitcoin [&#8230;]</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:175:<p>The post <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/us-lawmakers-push-new-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-act-to-secure-25-billion-federal-stash/\">US lawmakers push new Strategic Bitcoin Reserve act to secure $25 billion federal stash</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com\">CryptoSlate</a>.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-176-]]></description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-177-\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>A renewed push to solidify the United States’ foothold in the digital asset market emerged Thursday as lawmakers unveiled legislation to establish a formal strategic <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/coins/bitcoin/\">Bitcoin</a> reserve and consolidate the federal government's multibillion-dollar cryptocurrency stockpile.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-178-<p>Spearheaded by Representative Nick Begich, the American Reserve Modernization Act (ARMA) of 2026 mandates the creation of a secure <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/is-the-eu-bitcoin-race-starting-france-targets-420k-btc-as-germany-weighs-reserves/\">Bitcoin reserve</a> within the US Department of the Treasury, alongside a separate “Digital Asset Stockpile” for federally held, non-Bitcoin cryptocurrencies.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-179-<p>The legislation aims to provide a long-term structure to the government’s existing digital wealth, primarily amassed through law enforcement seizures. According to data from Bitcoin Treasuries, the <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/us-to-add-14-billion-btc-to-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-seized-from-chinese-scammer/\">US currently holds 328,372 Bitcoin</a>, a stash valued at more than $25 billion.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-180-<figure id=\"attachment_537689\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-537689\" style=\"width: 1093px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-537689\" src=\"https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Screenshot-2026-05-21-164126.jpg\" alt=\"US Government's Bitcoin Holdings\" width=\"1093\" height=\"595\" srcset=\"https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Screenshot-2026-05-21-164126.jpg 1093w, https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Screenshot-2026-05-21-164126-300x163.jpg 300w, https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Screenshot-2026-05-21-164126-1024x557.jpg 1024w, https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Screenshot-2026-05-21-164126-768x418.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1093px) 100vw, 1093px\" /><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-537689\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">US Government's Bitcoin Holdings (Source: Bitcoin Treasuries)</figcaption></figure>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-181-<p>Begich <a href=\"https://begich.house.gov/media/press-releases/congressman-nick-begich-leads-legislation-establish-strategic-bitcoin-reserve\">said</a> in a statement:</p>\n--\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-198-<p>However, these initiatives have considerably stalled despite the Trump administration's pro-crypto stance.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-199-<p>Still, the Begich bill aims to build on the recent <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/clarity-act-could-be-signed-into-law-by-president-donald-trump-in-early-august-galaxy-digital/\">advancement of the Clarity Act</a>, which passed the Senate Banking Committee with bipartisan support. That bill is designed to establish clear rules of the road for the industry and encourage institutional investment.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:200:<p>The post <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/us-lawmakers-push-new-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-act-to-secure-25-billion-federal-stash/\">US lawmakers push new Strategic Bitcoin Reserve act to secure $25 billion federal stash</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com\">CryptoSlate</a>.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-201-]]></content:encoded>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-202-\t\t\t\t\t\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-203-\t\t\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-204-\t\t\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-205-\t\t<media:content url=\"https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/us-bitcoin-reserve.jpg\" medium=\"image\"/>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-206-<enclosure url=\"https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/us-bitcoin-reserve.jpg\" length=\"1280\" type=\"image/jpg\"/>\n--\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml-59-  </item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml-60-  <item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml:61:    <title>US Lawmakers Introduce Bill to Establish Strategic Bitcoin Reserve</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml-62-    <link>https://cryptofox.news/news/us-lawmakers-introduce-bill-to-establish-strategic-bitcoin-reserve</link>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml-63-    <description>US Representative Nick Begich has introduced the Reserve Modernization Act, a legislative proposal designed to formalize the role of digital assets within the national treasury. Supported by 16 original co-sponsors, the bill seeks to establish a permanent strategic Bitcoin res…</description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml-64-    <category>Markets</category>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml-65-    <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>US Representative <strong>Nick Begich</strong> has introduced the <strong>Reserve Modernization Act</strong>, a legislative proposal designed to formalize the role of digital assets within the national treasury. Supported by <strong>16 original co-sponsors</strong>, the bill seeks to establish a permanent <strong>strategic Bitcoin reserve</strong>, integrating federally held digital assets into a long-term storage framework. This initiative marks a significant shift in federal fiscal policy, aiming to treat <strong>BTC</strong> as a cornerstone of the nation's financial security for the coming decades.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml-66-<h2>Legislative Framework and 20-Year Lock-In Period</h2>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml-67-<p>The proposed act focuses on the long-term preservation of digital assets. Under the terms of the legislation, any Bitcoin held within the strategic reserve would be <strong>locked for a minimum period of 20 years</strong>. This provision is intended to prevent short-term liquidation and ensure that the asset serves as a generational store of value. <em>By mandating a two-decade holding period, the bill aims to insulate the reserve from market volatility and shifting political priorities.</em></p>\n--\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml-99-  </item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml-100-  <item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml:101:    <title>US Lawmakers Introduce Bill to Establish Strategic Bitcoin Reserve</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml-102-    <link>https://cryptofox.news/news/us-lawmakers-introduce-bill-to-establish-strategic-bitcoin-reserve</link>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml-103-    <description>US Representative Nick Begich has introduced the Reserve Modernization Act, a legislative proposal designed to formalize the role of digital assets within the national treasury. Supported by 16 original co-sponsors, the bill seeks to establish a permanent strategic Bitcoin res…</description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml-104-    <category>Markets</category>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml-105-    <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>US Representative <strong>Nick Begich</strong> has introduced the <strong>Reserve Modernization Act</strong>, a legislative proposal designed to formalize the role of digital assets within the national treasury. Supported by <strong>16 original co-sponsors</strong>, the bill seeks to establish a permanent <strong>strategic Bitcoin reserve</strong>, integrating federally held digital assets into a long-term storage framework. This initiative marks a significant shift in federal fiscal policy, aiming to treat <strong>BTC</strong> as a cornerstone of the nation's financial security for the coming decades.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml-106-<h2>Legislative Framework and 20-Year Lock-In Period</h2>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml-107-<p>The proposed act focuses on the long-term preservation of digital assets. Under the terms of the legislation, any Bitcoin held within the strategic reserve would be <strong>locked for a minimum period of 20 years</strong>. This provision is intended to prevent short-term liquidation and ensure that the asset serves as a generational store of value. <em>By mandating a two-decade holding period, the bill aims to insulate the reserve from market volatility and shifting political priorities.</em></p>"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":73,"aggregated":"/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-79-    </item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-80-    <item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml:81:      <title>US lawmakers renew strategic Bitcoin reserve push with ARMA bill</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-82-      <pubDate>Fri, 22 May 2026 04:02:37 +0000</pubDate>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-83-      <atom:updated>Fri, 22 May 2026 04:02:37 +0000</atom:updated>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-84-      <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-senators-unveil-new-bitcoin-bill-renewing-strategic-reserve-plans</guid>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-85-      <link><![CDATA[https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-senators-unveil-new-bitcoin-bill-renewing-strategic-reserve-plans?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound]]></link>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml:86:      <description><![CDATA[<p style=\"float:right; margin:0 0 10px 15px; width:240px;\"><img src=\"https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy1pbWFnZXMuY3RtZWRpYS5pby9tZWRpYS9hcnRpY2xlLWNvdmVycy9oaS1uZXctdXMtY2hpZWYtb2Ytc3RhZmYtc3VwcG9ydHMtYml0Y29pbjEuanBn.jpg\" alt=\"US lawmakers renew strategic Bitcoin reserve push with ARMA bill\" class=\"type:primaryImage\"></p><p>Under the American Reserve Modernization Act of 2026, Bitcoin must be held for a minimum of 20 years unless used to slash national debt.</p>]]></description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-87-      <dc:creator>Cointelegraph by Brayden Lindrea</dc:creator>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-88-      <media:content url=\"https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy1pbWFnZXMuY3RtZWRpYS5pby9tZWRpYS9hcnRpY2xlLWNvdmVycy9oaS1uZXctdXMtY2hpZWYtb2Ytc3RhZmYtc3VwcG9ydHMtYml0Y29pbjEuanBn.jpg\" width=\"528\" medium=\"image\"/>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-89-      <enclosure url=\"https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy1pbWFnZXMuY3RtZWRpYS5pby9tZWRpYS9hcnRpY2xlLWNvdmVycy9oaS1uZXctdXMtY2hpZWYtb2Ytc3RhZmYtc3VwcG9ydHMtYml0Y29pbjEuanBn.jpg\" length=\"528\" type=\"image/jpg\"/>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-90-      <category>Latest News</category>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-91-    </item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cointelegraph.xml-92-    <item>\n--\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml-348-    \n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml-349-      <item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml:350:  <title>Proposed ARMA Bill Aims to Enshrine Strategic Bitcoin Reserve Into Law</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml-351-  <link>https://decrypt.co/368662/proposed-arma-bill-aims-enshrine-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-law</link>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml-352-  <pubDate>Thu, 21 May 2026 18:08:49 +0000</pubDate>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml-353-  \n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml-354-    <description>The American Reserve Modernization Act would direct the Treasury to create and maintain a Bitcoin reserve for a minimum of 20 years.</description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml-355-  \n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/decrypt.xml-356-  <dc:creator>André Beganski</dc:creator>\n--\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-155-\t</item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-156-\t\t<item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:157:\t\t<title>US lawmakers push new Strategic Bitcoin Reserve act to secure $25 billion federal stash</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-158-\t\t<link>https://cryptoslate.com/us-lawmakers-push-new-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-act-to-secure-25-billion-federal-stash/</link>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-159-\t\t\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-160-\t\t<dc:creator><![CDATA[Oluwapelumi Adejumo]]></dc:creator>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-161-\t\t<pubDate>Thu, 21 May 2026 19:05:23 +0000</pubDate>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-162-\t\t\t\t<category><![CDATA[Featured]]></category>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-163-\t\t<category><![CDATA[Legislation]]></category>\n--\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-173-\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-174-\t\t\t\t\t<description><![CDATA[<p>A renewed push to solidify the United States’ foothold in the digital asset market emerged Thursday as lawmakers unveiled legislation to establish a formal strategic Bitcoin reserve and consolidate the federal government's multibillion-dollar cryptocurrency stockpile. Spearheaded by Representative Nick Begich, the American Reserve Modernization Act (ARMA) of 2026 mandates the creation of a secure Bitcoin [&#8230;]</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:175:<p>The post <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/us-lawmakers-push-new-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-act-to-secure-25-billion-federal-stash/\">US lawmakers push new Strategic Bitcoin Reserve act to secure $25 billion federal stash</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com\">CryptoSlate</a>.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-176-]]></description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-177-\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>A renewed push to solidify the United States’ foothold in the digital asset market emerged Thursday as lawmakers unveiled legislation to establish a formal strategic <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/coins/bitcoin/\">Bitcoin</a> reserve and consolidate the federal government's multibillion-dollar cryptocurrency stockpile.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-178-<p>Spearheaded by Representative Nick Begich, the American Reserve Modernization Act (ARMA) of 2026 mandates the creation of a secure <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/is-the-eu-bitcoin-race-starting-france-targets-420k-btc-as-germany-weighs-reserves/\">Bitcoin reserve</a> within the US Department of the Treasury, alongside a separate “Digital Asset Stockpile” for federally held, non-Bitcoin cryptocurrencies.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-179-<p>The legislation aims to provide a long-term structure to the government’s existing digital wealth, primarily amassed through law enforcement seizures. According to data from Bitcoin Treasuries, the <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/us-to-add-14-billion-btc-to-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-seized-from-chinese-scammer/\">US currently holds 328,372 Bitcoin</a>, a stash valued at more than $25 billion.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-180-<figure id=\"attachment_537689\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-537689\" style=\"width: 1093px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-537689\" src=\"https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Screenshot-2026-05-21-164126.jpg\" alt=\"US Government's Bitcoin Holdings\" width=\"1093\" height=\"595\" srcset=\"https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Screenshot-2026-05-21-164126.jpg 1093w, https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Screenshot-2026-05-21-164126-300x163.jpg 300w, https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Screenshot-2026-05-21-164126-1024x557.jpg 1024w, https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Screenshot-2026-05-21-164126-768x418.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1093px) 100vw, 1093px\" /><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-537689\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">US Government's Bitcoin Holdings (Source: Bitcoin Treasuries)</figcaption></figure>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-181-<p>Begich <a href=\"https://begich.house.gov/media/press-releases/congressman-nick-begich-leads-legislation-establish-strategic-bitcoin-reserve\">said</a> in a statement:</p>\n--\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-198-<p>However, these initiatives have considerably stalled despite the Trump administration's pro-crypto stance.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-199-<p>Still, the Begich bill aims to build on the recent <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/clarity-act-could-be-signed-into-law-by-president-donald-trump-in-early-august-galaxy-digital/\">advancement of the Clarity Act</a>, which passed the Senate Banking Committee with bipartisan support. That bill is designed to establish clear rules of the road for the industry and encourage institutional investment.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml:200:<p>The post <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com/us-lawmakers-push-new-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-act-to-secure-25-billion-federal-stash/\">US lawmakers push new Strategic Bitcoin Reserve act to secure $25 billion federal stash</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://cryptoslate.com\">CryptoSlate</a>.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-201-]]></content:encoded>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-202-\t\t\t\t\t\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-203-\t\t\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-204-\t\t\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-205-\t\t<media:content url=\"https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/us-bitcoin-reserve.jpg\" medium=\"image\"/>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptoslate.xml-206-<enclosure url=\"https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/us-bitcoin-reserve.jpg\" length=\"1280\" type=\"image/jpg\"/>\n--\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml-59-  </item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml-60-  <item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml:61:    <title>US Lawmakers Introduce Bill to Establish Strategic Bitcoin Reserve</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml-62-    <link>https://cryptofox.news/news/us-lawmakers-introduce-bill-to-establish-strategic-bitcoin-reserve</link>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml-63-    <description>US Representative Nick Begich has introduced the Reserve Modernization Act, a legislative proposal designed to formalize the role of digital assets within the national treasury. Supported by 16 original co-sponsors, the bill seeks to establish a permanent strategic Bitcoin res…</description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml-64-    <category>Markets</category>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml-65-    <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>US Representative <strong>Nick Begich</strong> has introduced the <strong>Reserve Modernization Act</strong>, a legislative proposal designed to formalize the role of digital assets within the national treasury. Supported by <strong>16 original co-sponsors</strong>, the bill seeks to establish a permanent <strong>strategic Bitcoin reserve</strong>, integrating federally held digital assets into a long-term storage framework. This initiative marks a significant shift in federal fiscal policy, aiming to treat <strong>BTC</strong> as a cornerstone of the nation's financial security for the coming decades.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml-66-<h2>Legislative Framework and 20-Year Lock-In Period</h2>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_markets.xml-67-<p>The proposed act focuses on the long-term preservation of digital assets. Under the terms of the legislation, any Bitcoin held within the strategic reserve would be <strong>locked for a minimum period of 20 years</strong>. This provision is intended to prevent short-term liquidation and ensure that the asset serves as a generational store of value. <em>By mandating a two-decade holding period, the bill aims to insulate the reserve from market volatility and shifting political priorities.</em></p>\n--\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml-99-  </item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml-100-  <item>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml:101:    <title>US Lawmakers Introduce Bill to Establish Strategic Bitcoin Reserve</title>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml-102-    <link>https://cryptofox.news/news/us-lawmakers-introduce-bill-to-establish-strategic-bitcoin-reserve</link>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml-103-    <description>US Representative Nick Begich has introduced the Reserve Modernization Act, a legislative proposal designed to formalize the role of digital assets within the national treasury. Supported by 16 original co-sponsors, the bill seeks to establish a permanent strategic Bitcoin res…</description>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml-104-    <category>Markets</category>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml-105-    <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>US Representative <strong>Nick Begich</strong> has introduced the <strong>Reserve Modernization Act</strong>, a legislative proposal designed to formalize the role of digital assets within the national treasury. Supported by <strong>16 original co-sponsors</strong>, the bill seeks to establish a permanent <strong>strategic Bitcoin reserve</strong>, integrating federally held digital assets into a long-term storage framework. This initiative marks a significant shift in federal fiscal policy, aiming to treat <strong>BTC</strong> as a cornerstone of the nation's financial security for the coming decades.</p>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml-106-<h2>Legislative Framework and 20-Year Lock-In Period</h2>\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/feeds/cryptofox_regulation.xml-107-<p>The proposed act focuses on the long-term preservation of digital assets. Under the terms of the legislation, any Bitcoin held within the strategic reserve would be <strong>locked for a minimum period of 20 years</strong>. This provision is intended to prevent short-term liquidation and ensure that the asset serves as a generational store of value. <em>By mandating a two-decade holding period, the bill aims to insulate the reserve from market volatility and shifting political priorities.</em></p>","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779434776692}}
{"type":"message","id":"382e9b94","parentId":"3738cf20","timestamp":"2026-05-22T07:26:26.398Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_XqeAoK5bvrZ1XdRC4Ny577JA","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"trafilatura -u 'https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-senators-unveil-new-bitcoin-bill-renewing-strategic-reserve-plans' --output-format markdown | head -c 12000","yieldMs":12000,"timeout":60}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_BGnDnNdMjq6SFpavj9yLuEHZ","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"trafilatura -u 'https://decrypt.co/368662/proposed-arma-bill-aims-enshrine-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-law' --output-format markdown | head -c 12000","yieldMs":12000,"timeout":60}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ENgUkPeSLEKIAiUVdr2koYz7","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"trafilatura -u 'https://cryptoslate.com/us-lawmakers-push-new-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-act-to-secure-25-billion-federal-stash/' --output-format markdown | head -c 12000","yieldMs":12000,"timeout":60}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_OoTQPz7DFe0ifSHojR6z8n5G","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"trafilatura -u 'https://cryptofox.news/news/us-lawmakers-introduce-bill-to-establish-strategic-bitcoin-reserve' --output-format markdown | head -c 12000","yieldMs":12000,"timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":5134,"output":633,"cacheRead":62464,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":68231,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779434776702,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DiEYsoLx9wtz6vy53ZowD3eTKMGmN"}}
{"type":"message","id":"034d16c6","parentId":"382e9b94","timestamp":"2026-05-22T07:26:29.171Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_XqeAoK5bvrZ1XdRC4Ny577JA","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In an interview on Sunday, Patrick Witt, of the President’s Council of Advisors for Digital Assets, referred to ARMA as “Version 2” of the BITCOIN Act and said the White House has spent considerable time examining the legal implications of a Bitcoin reserve.\n\n“It's a breakthrough as far as getting everything in place, legally sound, properly safeguarding the assets.”\n\nThe push for a federal policy comes as the US currently holds 328,372 Bitcoin worth more than $25.5 billion — the most of any nation-state — but has sold portions of those holdings through court-ordered actions over the years.\n\n“The US is already one of the largest holders of Bitcoin in the world. But Congress has never set a federal policy on what to do with that asset,” said US Representative Jared Golden, one of the 16 co-sponsors of the bill.\n\nUnder ARMA, Bitcoin must be held for a minimum of 20 years unless it is sold to reduce America’s national debt, which topped $39 trillion on Wednesday.\n\nLike the BITCOIN Act, ARMA also seeks to acquire up to 1 million Bitcoin over five years through budget-neutral strategies, meaning it would avoid using taxpayer money.\n\nUS Representative Mike Carey argued that as digital assets continue to grow in importance, the bill could strengthen America’s long-term economic position and help keep it “competitive on the world stage.”\n\n**Related: ****SpaceX reveals larger-than-expected Bitcoin holdings in IPO filing**** **\n\nStrive CEO and chairman Matt Cole said ARMA is the “single most important crypto legislation” that could come out of Washington DC.\n\nQuarterly proof of reserve reports and independent third-party audits of the Bitcoin reserve would be published under ARMA, Begich noted.\n\nThe bill also seeks to protect digital property rights by affirming that the federal government may not impair the right of individuals to own or self-custody digital assets.\n\n**Magazine: ****eToro founder timed Bitcoin top perfectly due to belief in 4 year cycles**\n\nMore on the subject"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":1572,"aggregated":"In an interview on Sunday, Patrick Witt, of the President’s Council of Advisors for Digital Assets, referred to ARMA as “Version 2” of the BITCOIN Act and said the White House has spent considerable time examining the legal implications of a Bitcoin reserve.\n\n“It's a breakthrough as far as getting everything in place, legally sound, properly safeguarding the assets.”\n\nThe push for a federal policy comes as the US currently holds 328,372 Bitcoin worth more than $25.5 billion — the most of any nation-state — but has sold portions of those holdings through court-ordered actions over the years.\n\n“The US is already one of the largest holders of Bitcoin in the world. But Congress has never set a federal policy on what to do with that asset,” said US Representative Jared Golden, one of the 16 co-sponsors of the bill.\n\nUnder ARMA, Bitcoin must be held for a minimum of 20 years unless it is sold to reduce America’s national debt, which topped $39 trillion on Wednesday.\n\nLike the BITCOIN Act, ARMA also seeks to acquire up to 1 million Bitcoin over five years through budget-neutral strategies, meaning it would avoid using taxpayer money.\n\nUS Representative Mike Carey argued that as digital assets continue to grow in importance, the bill could strengthen America’s long-term economic position and help keep it “competitive on the world stage.”\n\n**Related: ****SpaceX reveals larger-than-expected Bitcoin holdings in IPO filing**** **\n\nStrive CEO and chairman Matt Cole said ARMA is the “single most important crypto legislation” that could come out of Washington DC.\n\nQuarterly proof of reserve reports and independent third-party audits of the Bitcoin reserve would be published under ARMA, Begich noted.\n\nThe bill also seeks to protect digital property rights by affirming that the federal government may not impair the right of individuals to own or self-custody digital assets.\n\n**Magazine: ****eToro founder timed Bitcoin top perfectly due to belief in 4 year cycles**\n\nMore on the subject","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779434789170}}
{"type":"message","id":"0df4df61","parentId":"034d16c6","timestamp":"2026-05-22T07:26:29.171Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_BGnDnNdMjq6SFpavj9yLuEHZ","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#### In brief\n\n- Reps. Nick Begich (R-AK) and Jared Golden (D-ME) introduced the American Reserve Modernization Act.\n- The bill seeks formally codify a strategic Bitcoin reserve into federal law, which would be managed for at least 20 years.\n- Aimed at cementing a core Trump administration promise, the initiative has faced ongoing hurdles.\n\nRep. Nick Begich (R-AK) introduced legislation on Thursday aimed at enshrining a strategic reserve for Bitcoin in federal law, seeking to cement one of President Donald Trump’s core campaign promises for digital asset holders ahead of the high-stakes U.S. midterm elections.\n\nThe American Reserve Modernization Act, or ARMA, would direct the Treasury Department to create and maintain a reserve of the digital asset for a minimum of 20 years, while establishing a stockpile for other cryptocurrencies held by the government.\n\nThe legislation also mandates the consolidation of what is believed to be billions of dollars in digital assets held across federal agencies—attained through actions like forfeitures and penalties—while providing transparency through a proof-of-reserve report.\n\nAs of last month, the strategic reserve for Bitcoin that Trump created via executive order is still a work in progress. At a conference in Las Vegas, Patrick Witt, executive director of the President’s Council of Advisors for Digital Assets, said the current administration has spent months “figuring out” the legal interpretations associated with the initiative.\n\nAmerica’s reserves balance sheet is a critical component of our nation’s insurance policy, bolstering our currency and providing assurance during times of uncertainty. Over time, the prevailing sentiment as to what constitutes a durable store of value can shift, and as such it is… pic.twitter.com/7XfBwAWFGi\n\n— Congressman Nick Begich (@RepNickBegich) May 21, 2026\n\n\nJoining Begich as the bill’s primary Democratic co-lead is Rep. Jared Golden (D-ME). The ARMA Act meanwhile counts 17 original co-sponsors, including Rep. Mike Collins (R-GA), among the first lawmakers to disclose an investment in a meme coin on Capitol Hill.\n\n“Administrations have auctioned [crypto] off or held it in reserve, according to the whims of the executive branch,” Golden said in a statement, noting that a stockpile created under the ARMA Act would enjoy the “weight of law.”\n\nAlthough a former administration official had said that the White House was eager to purchase as much Bitcoin as possible in a “budget-neutral way,” Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent later dented enthusiasm by ruling out any agency purchases.\n\nThe bill is aimed at providing the flexibility needed to broaden America’s portfolio of reserve assets that effectively serve as insurance policy, while also safeguarding crypto from “the whims of Congress or future administrations,” Begich said in an X post on Thursday.\n\nEstablished in May 2025 with a stroke of the president’s pen, the strategic reserve for Bitcoin was swiftly skewered by critics, including Rep. Maxine Waters (D-CA), the ranking member of the House Financial Services Committee, who warned of benefits for Trump insiders.\n\n“Typically, when the government holds strategic reserves, it is for an essential input that powers the U.S. economy and day-to-day life for American families,” she said. “Crypto, however, does not fall into these categories, because it has no inherent value.”\n\nAlthough the much-hyped stockpile’s creation represented a symbolic win for the digital assets industry, the government has yet to announce any allocations. Last year, Sen. Cynthia Lummis (R-WY) re-introduced the BITCOIN Act, a bill that directs the Treasury to purchase 1 million Bitcoin over five years in a way that seeks to avoid taxing citizens.\n\n*Decrypt* has reached out to Begich and Golden for comment."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":2415,"aggregated":"#### In brief\n\n- Reps. Nick Begich (R-AK) and Jared Golden (D-ME) introduced the American Reserve Modernization Act.\n- The bill seeks formally codify a strategic Bitcoin reserve into federal law, which would be managed for at least 20 years.\n- Aimed at cementing a core Trump administration promise, the initiative has faced ongoing hurdles.\n\nRep. Nick Begich (R-AK) introduced legislation on Thursday aimed at enshrining a strategic reserve for Bitcoin in federal law, seeking to cement one of President Donald Trump’s core campaign promises for digital asset holders ahead of the high-stakes U.S. midterm elections.\n\nThe American Reserve Modernization Act, or ARMA, would direct the Treasury Department to create and maintain a reserve of the digital asset for a minimum of 20 years, while establishing a stockpile for other cryptocurrencies held by the government.\n\nThe legislation also mandates the consolidation of what is believed to be billions of dollars in digital assets held across federal agencies—attained through actions like forfeitures and penalties—while providing transparency through a proof-of-reserve report.\n\nAs of last month, the strategic reserve for Bitcoin that Trump created via executive order is still a work in progress. At a conference in Las Vegas, Patrick Witt, executive director of the President’s Council of Advisors for Digital Assets, said the current administration has spent months “figuring out” the legal interpretations associated with the initiative.\n\nAmerica’s reserves balance sheet is a critical component of our nation’s insurance policy, bolstering our currency and providing assurance during times of uncertainty. Over time, the prevailing sentiment as to what constitutes a durable store of value can shift, and as such it is… pic.twitter.com/7XfBwAWFGi\n\n— Congressman Nick Begich (@RepNickBegich) May 21, 2026\n\n\nJoining Begich as the bill’s primary Democratic co-lead is Rep. Jared Golden (D-ME). The ARMA Act meanwhile counts 17 original co-sponsors, including Rep. Mike Collins (R-GA), among the first lawmakers to disclose an investment in a meme coin on Capitol Hill.\n\n“Administrations have auctioned [crypto] off or held it in reserve, according to the whims of the executive branch,” Golden said in a statement, noting that a stockpile created under the ARMA Act would enjoy the “weight of law.”\n\nAlthough a former administration official had said that the White House was eager to purchase as much Bitcoin as possible in a “budget-neutral way,” Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent later dented enthusiasm by ruling out any agency purchases.\n\nThe bill is aimed at providing the flexibility needed to broaden America’s portfolio of reserve assets that effectively serve as insurance policy, while also safeguarding crypto from “the whims of Congress or future administrations,” Begich said in an X post on Thursday.\n\nEstablished in May 2025 with a stroke of the president’s pen, the strategic reserve for Bitcoin was swiftly skewered by critics, including Rep. Maxine Waters (D-CA), the ranking member of the House Financial Services Committee, who warned of benefits for Trump insiders.\n\n“Typically, when the government holds strategic reserves, it is for an essential input that powers the U.S. economy and day-to-day life for American families,” she said. “Crypto, however, does not fall into these categories, because it has no inherent value.”\n\nAlthough the much-hyped stockpile’s creation represented a symbolic win for the digital assets industry, the government has yet to announce any allocations. Last year, Sen. Cynthia Lummis (R-WY) re-introduced the BITCOIN Act, a bill that directs the Treasury to purchase 1 million Bitcoin over five years in a way that seeks to avoid taxing citizens.\n\n*Decrypt* has reached out to Begich and Golden for comment.","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779434789171}}
{"type":"message","id":"36ad051b","parentId":"0df4df61","timestamp":"2026-05-22T07:26:29.171Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ENgUkPeSLEKIAiUVdr2koYz7","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# US lawmakers push new Strategic Bitcoin Reserve act to secure $25 billion federal stash\n\nARMA would force the government to hold its Bitcoin for two decades to build a strategic financial buffer.\n\nA renewed push to solidify the United States’ foothold in the digital asset market emerged Thursday as lawmakers unveiled legislation to establish a formal strategic Bitcoin reserve and consolidate the federal government's multibillion-dollar cryptocurrency stockpile.\n\nSpearheaded by Representative Nick Begich, the American Reserve Modernization Act (ARMA) of 2026 mandates the creation of a secure Bitcoin reserve within the US Department of the Treasury, alongside a separate “Digital Asset Stockpile” for federally held, non-Bitcoin cryptocurrencies.\n\nThe legislation aims to provide a long-term structure to the government’s existing digital wealth, primarily amassed through law enforcement seizures. According to data from Bitcoin Treasuries, the US currently holds 328,372 Bitcoin, a stash valued at more than $25 billion.\n\nBegich said in a statement:\n\n“The American Reserve Modernization Act positions the United States to lead confidently in the digital age while protecting taxpayer interests, strengthening financial sovereignty, and reinforcing the principles of transparency and sound stewardship.”\n\n\nThe bill has 17 original House co-sponsors, including Buddy Carter, Ben Cline of Virginia, Barry Moore of Alabama, Burgess Owens of Utah, Mariannette Miller-Meeks of Iowa, Mike Carey and Michael Rulli of Ohio, Mike Collins of Georgia, Mike Lawler of New York, Riley Moore of West Virginia, and Tim Moore of North Carolina.\n\nApart from the strong legislative support, crypto industry leaders are already throwing their weight behind the measure.\n\nMatt Cole, CEO of Bitcoin treasury firm Strive, called the proposal “the single most important crypto legislation that can come out of D.C.” for the long-term health and security of the United States.\n\n## ARMA establishes a 20-year Bitcoin bet\n\nIf enacted, the bill would radically alter how Washington handles digital assets. Rather than periodically auctioning off seized crypto, the Treasury would be forced to consolidate custody and oversight across all federal agencies.\n\nCrucially, the legislation requires that any Bitcoin held in the strategic reserve be maintained for at least 20 years, effectively turning the US government into a long-term “hodler.”\n\nTo address persistent industry demands for transparency, the bill establishes stringent reporting measures. The Treasury would be required to publish quarterly public “Proof of Reserve” reports, submit to independent third-party audits, and face direct congressional oversight.\n\nThe legislation also directs a study into budget-neutral acquisition strategies. The goal is to evaluate lawful methods for the government to expand its digital reserves without relying on tax increases, deficit spending, or adding to the national debt.\n\nFurthermore, the bill offers an olive branch to crypto advocates by explicitly protecting self-custody rights, affirming that the federal government may not impair Americans' lawful right to own, transfer, or independently secure their digital assets.\n\n## Mounting pro-Bitcoin momentum in Washington\n\nBegich’s proposal builds on a broader, ongoing effort in Washington to pivot the US toward a pro-crypto stance.\n\nLast year, Sen. Cynthia Lummis proposed the BITCOIN Act, which would require the United States to acquire 1 million Bitcoin over five years, hold the assets for at least 20 years, and distribute storage across secure sites nationwide.\n\nThe bill also includes a financing mechanism tied to Federal Reserve gold certificates, a structure that would make the proposal a direct bet on converting part of the federal balance sheet into Bitcoin exposure.\n\nLummis legislation followed President Donald Trump's executive order to establish a strategic Bitcoin reserve.\n\nHowever, these initiatives have considerably stalled despite the Trump administration's pro-crypto stance.\n\nStill, the Begich bill aims to build on the recent advancement of the Clarity Act, which passed the Senate Banking Committee with bipartisan support. That bill is designed to establish clear rules of the road for the industry and encourage institutional investment.\n\nBitcoin is **-0.25%** over the past 24 hours and currently sits at rank #1 by market cap.\n\n## Where the broader market sits right now\n\nRight now, the total crypto market is valued at **$2.58T** with **$77.13B** in 24-hour volume. Bitcoin dominance sits at **60.01%**. Explore the market"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":2082,"aggregated":"# US lawmakers push new Strategic Bitcoin Reserve act to secure $25 billion federal stash\n\nARMA would force the government to hold its Bitcoin for two decades to build a strategic financial buffer.\n\nA renewed push to solidify the United States’ foothold in the digital asset market emerged Thursday as lawmakers unveiled legislation to establish a formal strategic Bitcoin reserve and consolidate the federal government's multibillion-dollar cryptocurrency stockpile.\n\nSpearheaded by Representative Nick Begich, the American Reserve Modernization Act (ARMA) of 2026 mandates the creation of a secure Bitcoin reserve within the US Department of the Treasury, alongside a separate “Digital Asset Stockpile” for federally held, non-Bitcoin cryptocurrencies.\n\nThe legislation aims to provide a long-term structure to the government’s existing digital wealth, primarily amassed through law enforcement seizures. According to data from Bitcoin Treasuries, the US currently holds 328,372 Bitcoin, a stash valued at more than $25 billion.\n\nBegich said in a statement:\n\n“The American Reserve Modernization Act positions the United States to lead confidently in the digital age while protecting taxpayer interests, strengthening financial sovereignty, and reinforcing the principles of transparency and sound stewardship.”\n\n\nThe bill has 17 original House co-sponsors, including Buddy Carter, Ben Cline of Virginia, Barry Moore of Alabama, Burgess Owens of Utah, Mariannette Miller-Meeks of Iowa, Mike Carey and Michael Rulli of Ohio, Mike Collins of Georgia, Mike Lawler of New York, Riley Moore of West Virginia, and Tim Moore of North Carolina.\n\nApart from the strong legislative support, crypto industry leaders are already throwing their weight behind the measure.\n\nMatt Cole, CEO of Bitcoin treasury firm Strive, called the proposal “the single most important crypto legislation that can come out of D.C.” for the long-term health and security of the United States.\n\n## ARMA establishes a 20-year Bitcoin bet\n\nIf enacted, the bill would radically alter how Washington handles digital assets. Rather than periodically auctioning off seized crypto, the Treasury would be forced to consolidate custody and oversight across all federal agencies.\n\nCrucially, the legislation requires that any Bitcoin held in the strategic reserve be maintained for at least 20 years, effectively turning the US government into a long-term “hodler.”\n\nTo address persistent industry demands for transparency, the bill establishes stringent reporting measures. The Treasury would be required to publish quarterly public “Proof of Reserve” reports, submit to independent third-party audits, and face direct congressional oversight.\n\nThe legislation also directs a study into budget-neutral acquisition strategies. The goal is to evaluate lawful methods for the government to expand its digital reserves without relying on tax increases, deficit spending, or adding to the national debt.\n\nFurthermore, the bill offers an olive branch to crypto advocates by explicitly protecting self-custody rights, affirming that the federal government may not impair Americans' lawful right to own, transfer, or independently secure their digital assets.\n\n## Mounting pro-Bitcoin momentum in Washington\n\nBegich’s proposal builds on a broader, ongoing effort in Washington to pivot the US toward a pro-crypto stance.\n\nLast year, Sen. Cynthia Lummis proposed the BITCOIN Act, which would require the United States to acquire 1 million Bitcoin over five years, hold the assets for at least 20 years, and distribute storage across secure sites nationwide.\n\nThe bill also includes a financing mechanism tied to Federal Reserve gold certificates, a structure that would make the proposal a direct bet on converting part of the federal balance sheet into Bitcoin exposure.\n\nLummis legislation followed President Donald Trump's executive order to establish a strategic Bitcoin reserve.\n\nHowever, these initiatives have considerably stalled despite the Trump administration's pro-crypto stance.\n\nStill, the Begich bill aims to build on the recent advancement of the Clarity Act, which passed the Senate Banking Committee with bipartisan support. That bill is designed to establish clear rules of the road for the industry and encourage institutional investment.\n\nBitcoin is **-0.25%** over the past 24 hours and currently sits at rank #1 by market cap.\n\n## Where the broader market sits right now\n\nRight now, the total crypto market is valued at **$2.58T** with **$77.13B** in 24-hour volume. Bitcoin dominance sits at **60.01%**. Explore the market","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779434789171}}
{"type":"message","id":"fd63d08a","parentId":"36ad051b","timestamp":"2026-05-22T07:26:29.177Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_OoTQPz7DFe0ifSHojR6z8n5G","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"US Representative **Nick Begich** has introduced the **Reserve Modernization Act**, a legislative proposal designed to formalize the role of digital assets within the national treasury. Supported by **16 original co-sponsors**, the bill seeks to establish a permanent **strategic Bitcoin reserve**, integrating federally held digital assets into a long-term storage framework. This initiative marks a significant shift in federal fiscal policy, aiming to treat **BTC** as a cornerstone of the nation's financial security for the coming decades.\n\n## Legislative Framework and 20-Year Lock-In Period\n\nThe proposed act focuses on the long-term preservation of digital assets. Under the terms of the legislation, any Bitcoin held within the strategic reserve would be **locked for a minimum period of 20 years**. This provision is intended to prevent short-term liquidation and ensure that the asset serves as a generational store of value. *By mandating a two-decade holding period, the bill aims to insulate the reserve from market volatility and shifting political priorities.*\n\nThe bill also outlines strategies for the **integration of existing federally held digital assets**, which often originate from law enforcement seizures. Rather than auctioning these assets, the government would transition them into the sovereign reserve.\n\n## Budget Neutrality and Legal Protections\n\nA key component of the Reserve Modernization Act is its focus on **budget-neutral acquisition strategies**. Lawmakers are exploring methods to expand the Bitcoin holdings without increasing the national deficit or requiring new taxpayer funding. Furthermore, the bill includes specific legal safeguards to:\n\n- Protect the reserve from\n**future liquidation efforts**by subsequent administrations. - Establish clear jurisdictional oversight for the management of the\n**blockchain-based assets**. - Codify the reserve into\n**official law**, providing a more permanent foundation than previous executive orders.\n\n*While prior administrative actions had moved toward creating a reserve through executive authority, this legislative approach seeks to provide a statutory mandate that would be significantly harder to reverse.*\n\nIn conclusion, the introduction of the Reserve Modernization Act on **May 22, 2026**, represents a major step toward the institutionalization of cryptocurrency at the federal level. By proposing a mandatory holding period and budget-neutral growth, the bill aims to stabilize the national balance sheet through the inclusion of decentralized assets. The progress of this legislation will be closely monitored by global markets as an indicator of the United States' long-term stance on **digital finance** and sovereign asset management.\n\n## Frequently Asked *Questions*\n\nQuick answers to the most common questions about this topic."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":2653,"aggregated":"US Representative **Nick Begich** has introduced the **Reserve Modernization Act**, a legislative proposal designed to formalize the role of digital assets within the national treasury. Supported by **16 original co-sponsors**, the bill seeks to establish a permanent **strategic Bitcoin reserve**, integrating federally held digital assets into a long-term storage framework. This initiative marks a significant shift in federal fiscal policy, aiming to treat **BTC** as a cornerstone of the nation's financial security for the coming decades.\n\n## Legislative Framework and 20-Year Lock-In Period\n\nThe proposed act focuses on the long-term preservation of digital assets. Under the terms of the legislation, any Bitcoin held within the strategic reserve would be **locked for a minimum period of 20 years**. This provision is intended to prevent short-term liquidation and ensure that the asset serves as a generational store of value. *By mandating a two-decade holding period, the bill aims to insulate the reserve from market volatility and shifting political priorities.*\n\nThe bill also outlines strategies for the **integration of existing federally held digital assets**, which often originate from law enforcement seizures. Rather than auctioning these assets, the government would transition them into the sovereign reserve.\n\n## Budget Neutrality and Legal Protections\n\nA key component of the Reserve Modernization Act is its focus on **budget-neutral acquisition strategies**. Lawmakers are exploring methods to expand the Bitcoin holdings without increasing the national deficit or requiring new taxpayer funding. Furthermore, the bill includes specific legal safeguards to:\n\n- Protect the reserve from\n**future liquidation efforts**by subsequent administrations. - Establish clear jurisdictional oversight for the management of the\n**blockchain-based assets**. - Codify the reserve into\n**official law**, providing a more permanent foundation than previous executive orders.\n\n*While prior administrative actions had moved toward creating a reserve through executive authority, this legislative approach seeks to provide a statutory mandate that would be significantly harder to reverse.*\n\nIn conclusion, the introduction of the Reserve Modernization Act on **May 22, 2026**, represents a major step toward the institutionalization of cryptocurrency at the federal level. By proposing a mandatory holding period and budget-neutral growth, the bill aims to stabilize the national balance sheet through the inclusion of decentralized assets. The progress of this legislation will be closely monitored by global markets as an indicator of the United States' long-term stance on **digital finance** and sovereign asset management.\n\n## Frequently Asked *Questions*\n\nQuick answers to the most common questions about this topic.","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779434789171}}
{"type":"message","id":"8545b1cf","parentId":"fd63d08a","timestamp":"2026-05-22T07:27:00.764Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_7zkT8Y0nW9bUwfffOi2hpwMC","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-072258/research/raw.json","content":"{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"story_id\": \"us-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-arma-bill-2026-05-22\",\n  \"topic_theme\": \"US lawmakers revive strategic Bitcoin reserve push with the ARMA bill\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"strategic Bitcoin reserve\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"US lawmakers renew strategic Bitcoin reserve push with ARMA bill\",\n  \"primary_asset\": \"Bitcoin\",\n  \"chart_coin\": \"bitcoin\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"Cointelegraph\",\n    \"Decrypt\",\n    \"CryptoSlate\",\n    \"CryptoFox\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-senators-unveil-new-bitcoin-bill-renewing-strategic-reserve-plans\",\n    \"https://decrypt.co/368662/proposed-arma-bill-aims-enshrine-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-law\",\n    \"https://cryptoslate.com/us-lawmakers-push-new-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-act-to-secure-25-billion-federal-stash/\",\n    \"https://cryptofox.news/news/us-lawmakers-introduce-bill-to-establish-strategic-bitcoin-reserve\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"Representative Nick Begich introduced the American Reserve Modernization Act (ARMA) to put a US strategic Bitcoin reserve into federal law, with Democratic Representative Jared Golden also backing the effort.\",\n    \"The bill would direct the Treasury Department to create a formal Bitcoin reserve and a separate digital asset stockpile for non-Bitcoin crypto already held by the government.\",\n    \"ARMA would require Bitcoin in the reserve to be held for at least 20 years, with Cointelegraph reporting the main explicit exception as sales used to reduce the national debt.\",\n    \"CryptoSlate says the US currently holds about 328,372 BTC worth more than $25 billion, while Cointelegraph cites more than $25.5 billion, making the existing stash the core asset base for the proposal.\",\n    \"Cointelegraph reports ARMA also seeks to acquire up to 1 million Bitcoin over five years through budget-neutral strategies designed to avoid taxpayer funding.\",\n    \"The legislation includes quarterly proof-of-reserve disclosures, independent third-party audits, and stronger statutory protections against future administrations simply changing course by executive preference.\",\n    \"The bill also explicitly protects lawful self-custody and digital property rights, signaling that the reserve push is paired with broader pro-crypto policy language rather than only government accumulation.\"\n  ],\n  \"tweet_quotes\": [],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"[Cointelegraph]\\nIn an interview on Sunday, Patrick Witt, of the President’s Council of Advisors for Digital Assets, referred to ARMA as ‘Version 2’ of the BITCOIN Act and said the White House has spent considerable time examining the legal implications of a Bitcoin reserve. ‘It's a breakthrough as far as getting everything in place, legally sound, properly safeguarding the assets.’ The push for a federal policy comes as the US currently holds 328,372 Bitcoin worth more than $25.5 billion — the most of any nation-state — but has sold portions of those holdings through court-ordered actions over the years. ‘The US is already one of the largest holders of Bitcoin in the world. But Congress has never set a federal policy on what to do with that asset,’ said US Representative Jared Golden, one of the 16 co-sponsors of the bill. Under ARMA, Bitcoin must be held for a minimum of 20 years unless it is sold to reduce America’s national debt, which topped $39 trillion on Wednesday. Like the BITCOIN Act, ARMA also seeks to acquire up to 1 million Bitcoin over five years through budget-neutral strategies, meaning it would avoid using taxpayer money. US Representative Mike Carey argued that as digital assets continue to grow in importance, the bill could strengthen America’s long-term economic position and help keep it ‘competitive on the world stage.’ Strive CEO and chairman Matt Cole said ARMA is the ‘single most important crypto legislation’ that could come out of Washington DC. Quarterly proof of reserve reports and independent third-party audits of the Bitcoin reserve would be published under ARMA, Begich noted. The bill also seeks to protect digital property rights by affirming that the federal government may not impair the right of individuals to own or self-custody digital assets.\\n\\n[Decrypt]\\nIn brief: Reps. Nick Begich (R-AK) and Jared Golden (D-ME) introduced the American Reserve Modernization Act. The bill seeks formally codify a strategic Bitcoin reserve into federal law, which would be managed for at least 20 years. Aimed at cementing a core Trump administration promise, the initiative has faced ongoing hurdles. Rep. Nick Begich introduced legislation on Thursday aimed at enshrining a strategic reserve for Bitcoin in federal law, seeking to cement one of President Donald Trump’s core campaign promises for digital asset holders ahead of the high-stakes U.S. midterm elections. The American Reserve Modernization Act, or ARMA, would direct the Treasury Department to create and maintain a reserve of the digital asset for a minimum of 20 years, while establishing a stockpile for other cryptocurrencies held by the government. The legislation also mandates the consolidation of what is believed to be billions of dollars in digital assets held across federal agencies—attained through actions like forfeitures and penalties—while providing transparency through a proof-of-reserve report. As of last month, the strategic reserve for Bitcoin that Trump created via executive order is still a work in progress. At a conference in Las Vegas, Patrick Witt, executive director of the President’s Council of Advisors for Digital Assets, said the current administration has spent months ‘figuring out’ the legal interpretations associated with the initiative. Joining Begich as the bill’s primary Democratic co-lead is Rep. Jared Golden. The ARMA Act meanwhile counts 17 original co-sponsors, including Rep. Mike Collins (R-GA), among the first lawmakers to disclose an investment in a meme coin on Capitol Hill. ‘Administrations have auctioned [crypto] off or held it in reserve, according to the whims of the executive branch,’ Golden said in a statement, noting that a stockpile created under the ARMA Act would enjoy the ‘weight of law.’ Although a former administration official had said that the White House was eager to purchase as much Bitcoin as possible in a ‘budget-neutral way,’ Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent later dented enthusiasm by ruling out any agency purchases. The bill is aimed at providing the flexibility needed to broaden America’s portfolio of reserve assets that effectively serve as insurance policy, while also safeguarding crypto from ‘the whims of Congress or future administrations,’ Begich said in an X post. Critics such as Maxine Waters argued that crypto does not meet the usual standard for strategic reserve assets.\\n\\n[CryptoSlate]\\nUS lawmakers push new Strategic Bitcoin Reserve act to secure $25 billion federal stash. ARMA would force the government to hold its Bitcoin for two decades to build a strategic financial buffer. A renewed push to solidify the United States’ foothold in the digital asset market emerged Thursday as lawmakers unveiled legislation to establish a formal strategic Bitcoin reserve and consolidate the federal government's multibillion-dollar cryptocurrency stockpile. Spearheaded by Representative Nick Begich, the American Reserve Modernization Act of 2026 mandates the creation of a secure Bitcoin reserve within the US Department of the Treasury, alongside a separate ‘Digital Asset Stockpile’ for federally held, non-Bitcoin cryptocurrencies. The legislation aims to provide a long-term structure to the government’s existing digital wealth, primarily amassed through law enforcement seizures. According to data from Bitcoin Treasuries, the US currently holds 328,372 Bitcoin, a stash valued at more than $25 billion. Begich said the act positions the United States to lead confidently in the digital age while protecting taxpayer interests, strengthening financial sovereignty, and reinforcing transparency and stewardship. The bill has broad House support, with more than 16 original co-sponsors listed. If enacted, the bill would radically alter how Washington handles digital assets. Rather than periodically auctioning off seized crypto, the Treasury would be forced to consolidate custody and oversight across all federal agencies. Crucially, the legislation requires that any Bitcoin held in the strategic reserve be maintained for at least 20 years, effectively turning the US government into a long-term ‘hodler.’ To address industry demands for transparency, the bill establishes quarterly public proof-of-reserve reports, independent third-party audits, and direct congressional oversight. The legislation also directs a study into budget-neutral acquisition strategies, explicitly exploring ways to expand reserves without tax increases, deficit spending, or adding to the national debt. It also protects self-custody rights, affirming that the federal government may not impair Americans’ lawful right to own, transfer, or independently secure their digital assets. CryptoSlate frames the measure as part of mounting pro-Bitcoin momentum in Washington and a legislative follow-on to the strategic reserve executive order and earlier Lummis BITCOIN Act proposals.\\n\\n[CryptoFox]\\nUS Representative Nick Begich has introduced the Reserve Modernization Act, a legislative proposal designed to formalize the role of digital assets within the national treasury. Supported by 16 original co-sponsors, the bill seeks to establish a permanent strategic Bitcoin reserve, integrating federally held digital assets into a long-term storage framework. This initiative marks a significant shift in federal fiscal policy, aiming to treat BTC as a cornerstone of the nation's financial security for the coming decades. The proposed act focuses on the long-term preservation of digital assets. Under the terms of the legislation, any Bitcoin held within the strategic reserve would be locked for a minimum period of 20 years. This provision is intended to prevent short-term liquidation and ensure that the asset serves as a generational store of value. The bill also outlines strategies for the integration of existing federally held digital assets, which often originate from law enforcement seizures. Rather than auctioning these assets, the government would transition them into the sovereign reserve. A key component of the Reserve Modernization Act is its focus on budget-neutral acquisition strategies. Lawmakers are exploring methods to expand the Bitcoin holdings without increasing the national deficit or requiring new taxpayer funding. The bill includes legal safeguards to protect the reserve from future liquidation efforts by subsequent administrations, establish clear jurisdictional oversight for management of blockchain-based assets, and codify the reserve into official law, creating a more permanent foundation than executive action alone. CryptoFox concludes that the bill represents a major step toward institutionalizing cryptocurrency at the federal level and that markets will watch it as a signal of the United States’ long-term stance on digital finance and sovereign asset management.\"\n}"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":3275,"output":2741,"cacheRead":67456,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":73472,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779434789178,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DiEZ5qZSNET3CKWjZ1fJmEZzxTX36"}}
